PRIVATE REFLECTION: {The poem is Sidney’s double sestina “Ye Goatherd Gods.”  Its canonical 12-stanza + 3-line envoi form is governed by the fixed 6-word rotation (A=mountains, B=valleys, C=forests, D=music, E=morning, F=evening) and by the requirement that the envoi read exactly:

These mountains witness shall, so shall these valleys;  
These forests eke, made wretched by our music;  
Our morning hymn is this, and song at evening.

In the supplied text only two lines violate both the rotation and the envoi template simultaneously: line 25 (“These forests eke…music”) belongs in the envoi, while line 74 (“Long since, alas…music”) belongs at the head of stanza 5.  Swapping precisely those two lines restores every stanza’s end-word sequence, the grammatical continuity of stanza 5, and the canonical envoi without affecting any other line.  All other proposed pairs (13/19, 15/21, 21/25, 25/28, 25/31, 25/73, 26/28, 26/75, 7/19) either break the rotation, leave the envoi malformed, or create new syntactic anomalies.  Hence the unique minimal repair is 25 and 74.}

